KG42.register("rules-a7668269610ddf821b551e28",{"id":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market::v141-c-R004","paper":"48-multiple_energy_carrier_market","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R004","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Social-welfare clearing objective","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"Demand submissions provide bid inputs to the welfare-maximizing market-clearing optimization. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction. Supply submissions provide bid inputs to the welfare-maximizing market-clearing optimization. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction. The clearing objective maximizes consumer and producer surplus, defined as the total valuation of cleared demand bids minus the total valuation of cleared supply bids. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.social_welfare under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","clearing.social_welfare"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"clearing.social_welfare","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"clearing.social_welfare","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R004-x-y_b","symbol":"y_b","meaning":"Amount cleared from bid b; source shorthand for y_{b,t,e,l}. The optimization variable in the social-welfare objective.","kind":"operational","domain":"0 \\le y_b \\le q_b, \\; \\forall b \\in B (nonnegative cleared amount bounded by the bid quantity; the upper bound is clearing constraint (2)).","unit":"kWh","indices":["b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E024"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R004-theta-v_b","symbol":"v_b","meaning":"Bid valuation for bid b; source shorthand for v_{b,t,e,l}. Coefficient on cleared demand and supply quantities in Eq. (1).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency/kWh (the supplied text layer omits the currency glyph; E002 shows '[ /kWh]' and v141-b-g02-E01 states 'öre/kWh')","indices":["b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E023"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R004-theta-q_b","symbol":"q_b","meaning":"Bid quantity for bid b; source shorthand for q_{b,t,e,l}. Upper bound on y_b in the clearing quantity constraint (2).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kWh","indices":["b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E001","v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E024"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Demand submissions provide bid inputs to the welfare-maximizing market-clearing optimization. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply submissions provide bid inputs to the welfare-maximizing market-clearing optimization. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The clearing objective maximizes consumer and producer surplus, defined as the total valuation of cleared demand bids minus the total valuation of cleared supply bids. Scope: Market-clearing optimization of the proposed local multi-energy-carrier auction.","expression":"\\max_{y_b}\\left[\\sum_{b\\in D} v_b \\cdot y_b - \\sum_{b\\in S} v_b \\cdot y_b\\right]","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R004-x-y_b"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R004-theta-v_b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g01-E001","v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E022"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E022","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 re 4.2. Market clearing and pricing re This se","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"This section provides a mathematical description of the market clearing mechanism, including all the main ingredients discussed in Section 4.1. The market clearing is based on mathematical optimization, where the objective is to maximize the sum of consumer and producer surplus. The problem is kept linear, which means that it can be solved efficiently using available linear programming (LP) software. Input to the market clearing problem consists of bids and bid dependencies, and outputs are the cleared bid quantities and market prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E023","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a 4.2.1. Objective and bid dependencies m The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize ","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize consumer and producer surplus, i.e. the difference between the sum of the valuations of all cleared demand bids and the sum of the valuations of all cleared supply bids. The optimization variables are y_b, denoting the amount to clear from each bid. \\max_{y_b} \\left[ \\sum_{b \\in D} v_b \\cdot y_b - \\sum_{b \\in S} v_b \\cdot y_b \\right] \\tag{1}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E001","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p02-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"M. Brolin and H. Pihl Nomenclature L0 Ll Algebraic symbols vb qb B , b set and index of bids Q D , d","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"B, b set and index of bids; D, d set and index of demand bids, D ⊂ B; S, s set and index of supply bids, S ⊂ B; R, r set and index of bid dependencies; R^X set of bid dependencies of type X, R^X ⊂ R; T, t set and index of time steps; E, e set and index of energy carriers; L, l set and index of pricing locations."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E002","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p02-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Electrical Power and Energy Systems 118 (2020) 105739 L0 set of reference locations, L0 ⊂ L Ll set o","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"L^0 set of reference locations, L^0 ⊂ L; L^l set of locations connected to pricing location l; v_{b,t,e,l} bid valuation [€/kWh]; q_{b,t,e,l} bid quantity [kWh]; Q_r total quantity for bid dependency [kWh]; y_{b,t,e,l} amount cleared from bid [kWh]; a_{l,k} admittance between locations [kW]; c_{l,k} transfer limit [kW]; inj_{t,e,l} net energy injection [kW]; flo_{t,e,l} net energy outflow [kW]; ang_{t,e,l} voltage angle [·]; λ_{t,e,l} market clearing price [€/kWh]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E024","location":{"location_id":"src-ec182c21f1-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a 4.2.1. Objective and bid dependencies m The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize ","equation_id":"(2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The amount to clear from each bid should be non-negative and cannot exceed the bid quantity: 0 \\leqslant y_b \\leqslant q_b, \\quad \\forall b \\in B. \\tag{2}"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.social_welfare","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E022","quote":"Input to the market clearing problem consists of bids and bid dependencies, and outputs are the cleared bid quantities and market prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E023","quote":"The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize consumer and producer surplus, i.e. the difference between the sum of the valuations of all cleared demand bids and the sum of the valuations of all cleared supply bids."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E022","quote":"Input to the market clearing problem consists of bids and bid dependencies, and outputs are the cleared bid quantities and market prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E023","quote":"The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize consumer and producer surplus, i.e. the difference between the sum of the valuations of all cleared demand bids and the sum of the valuations of all cleared supply bids."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E023","quote":"The objective for the optimization problem is to maximize consumer and producer surplus, i.e. the difference between the sum of the valuations of all cleared demand bids and the sum of the valuations of all cleared supply bids."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"cb88eb9e4f72606abe185de0dc15744f23a716477f65a406ae0af040631c5071","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Eq. (1) in v141-b-g01-E023 gives an explicit optimization objective; the source defines y_b as the amount cleared from each bid (E002/E023), v_b as the bid valuation (E002), and D and S as the demand and supply bid sets (E001). The expression is transcribed with the source signs and index sets. C001 and C002 remain procedural input-role statements because they do not state algebraic constraints. B evidence is unreviewed; the currency glyph in the unit of v_b is not recoverable from the text layer, and the source uses the shorthand v_b,y_b for v_{b,t,e,l},y_{b,t,e,l}. The domain upper bound y_b \u003c= q_b comes from clearing constraint (2) (E024), which is outside this rule's frozen phi set but is the same source mechanism.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-x-y_b","node_ids":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001","v141-c-R004-E002"],"rationale":"y_b is the amount cleared from each bid. It is defined for demand bids D and supply bids S, which enter the social-welfare objective through E001 and E002; the objective node is clearing.social_welfare."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-theta-v_b","node_ids":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001","v141-c-R004-E002"],"rationale":"v_b is the bid valuation coefficient that weights cleared demand and supply quantities in Eq. (1). E001 and E002 carry the demand and supply bid inputs into the welfare objective."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-theta-q_b","node_ids":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"q_b is a bid quantity attribute of demand and supply bids and bounds y_b; the frozen rule has no edge specifically representing bid quantity, so no edge is claimed."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001","v141-c-R004-E002"],"rationale":"C003 is the formal welfare objective at clearing.social_welfare, aggregating demand and supply bid valuations through the two frozen links."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
